Quarterly and after every access change:

1. list GitHub owners, collaborators, installed Apps, deploy keys, Actions permissions, environment reviewers, secrets, and rulesets;
2. list Cloudflare members, API tokens, token scopes, Workers, routes, custom domains, environment variables, and rollback access;
3. list Turnstile and email-provider keys and authorized users;
4. remove stale users, tokens, Apps, keys, and broad scopes;
5. rotate credentials whose ownership or history is unclear;
6. confirm PR jobs cannot read deployment secrets;
7. confirm preview, staging, and production use separate least-privilege tokens;
8. record reviewer, date, findings, remediation owner, and due date without recording secret values.

Current repository files cannot prove external access state. The first review remains required before CI/CD activation.
